<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The app's own spacing tokens. One declaration each, never a literal copied into a layout or
     style (the rule #380/#381/#384/#408/#424 closed).

     NO bottom_nav_* token lives here any more (#531). The bottom nav is libs:bottomnav's island
     and its geometry is declared once, in that module's res/values/dimens.xml. A same-named
     dimen here would silently OVERRIDE the library's at resource merge, which is a second
     declaration of every number #462/#473/#477/#498 settled. BottomNavGeometryTest reads the
     library's tokens back and fails if the rendered island disagrees with them. -->

<resources>
    <!-- #477 / #573. EVERY tab strip's vertical geometry, declared ONCE and
         applied by AppTabsStyle.apply — the section strips, Profile's,
         Launcher's, the drawer's. Until #573 only SectionTabsFragment read the
         top base, so a page's own strip sat higher than a section's.

         tab_strip_top_inset is the strip's OWN top breathing room above the
         toolbar island the app draws INTO the camera cutout. A base only: the
         real clearance is added at runtime from the status-bar / display-cutout
         inset (AppTabsStyle installs the insets listener and sets the strip's
         top margin to base + inset), because a fixed dp is right at one cutout
         geometry and wrong at every other — the #407 rule the launcher clock
         already follows.

         tab_strip_bottom_inset is the gap between the strip and the page below
         it, the same on every page. The two are equal on purpose: the strip
         breathes the same above and below. -->
    <dimen name="tab_strip_top_inset">10dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tab_strip_bottom_inset">10dp</dimen>
</resources>